C++ API
=======

The stable TSL 1.x C++ surface consists of the declarations reachable through
``tsl.hpp`` in namespace ``tsl``: vector and span types, primitive wrappers and
their checked companions, ``dataparallel`` policies, and public ``algo``
functions and policy tags. Physical profile headers, ``detail`` namespaces,
and compiler-selection macros are implementation details.

Unsuffixed calls do not validate dynamic preconditions. The checked contract,
error-output convention, residual C++ object obligations, and a compiled
example are described in :doc:`checked_api_contract`.

